@startuml ddc_recovery_state
' Created 2026-05-13: per claudeit/_diagram_amendments.md
!include dark-theme.puml
title DDC recovery state machine\nOwned by DDCRecoveryService; transitions verified at commit 4b5600b

' Per-monitor recovery state lives on MonitorInfo (SliderState + IsReadDegraded)
state Healthy : SliderState != Failed\n!IsReadDegraded
state Failed : SliderState == Failed\nLastDDCError set\n_entries.Remove, _writeThrottler.Drop
state ReadDegraded : SliderState != Failed\nIsReadDegraded == true\nSlider operable, reads fail
state Abandoned : RecoveryAttempts >= MaxRecoveryAttempts\nMonitorAbandoned event raised\nUI surfaces "gave up" badge

[*] --> Healthy

Healthy --> Failed : DoBrightnessWriteAsync exhausted (:1769-1784)\nOR VerifyAppliedAsync exhausted (:1822-1882)\nOR Refresh re-probe failure (:603-612)\nOR WasEverDDCCapable monitor disappeared (:475-491)

Failed --> Healthy : PromoteRecovered (:1463-1517)\n(read succeeded)
Failed --> ReadDegraded : PromoteReadDegraded (:1361-1389)\n(read failed but TryDDCWriteProbe succeeded)
Failed --> Failed : both probes failed, refresh LastDDCError
Failed --> Abandoned : attempts >= AppSettings.MaxRecoveryAttempts
ReadDegraded --> Abandoned : attempts >= AppSettings.MaxRecoveryAttempts

ReadDegraded --> Healthy : reads come back -> PromoteRecovered
ReadDegraded --> Failed : writes start failing\n(BeginInvoke at :1295-1312)

note bottom of Failed
  DDCRecoveryService.OnTick (1 s) consumes Failed and ReadDegraded as
  candidates via GetStuckRecoveryCandidateIds:1162.
  PickAction (:177-189):
    attempts 1..3   -> Probe
    attempts 4..6   -> RefreshHandle
    attempts 7..    -> alternate (attempt%2==0)?RefreshHandle:Probe
  Per-monitor post-detection settle now gates the next attempt (H-31),
  giving the panel a chance to stabilize after a topology-driven
  failure burst before the next probe.
  Independent: every 30 s the OnTick gate opens for rate-limited
  full Refresh.
end note

note bottom of Abandoned
  Terminal state at AppSettings.MaxRecoveryAttempts (default 60).
  MonitorAbandoned event signals the UI so the row can show the
  user-visible "gave up" indicator and stop the runaway probe loop.
  Recovery resumes if the user re-triggers (manual refresh, topology
  change, app restart) which resets RecoveryAttempts.
end note

note bottom of ReadDegraded
  ReadDegraded monitors STAY candidates so probes continue to test reads.
  TryDDCWriteProbe (MonitorService.cs:1332-1350) writes const ProbeRaw=50
  (an in-range raw VCP value, no scaling dependency on entry.Max).
  Safe across Max=100 and Max=255 panels.
end note

' Primitives explicitly NOT present (verified absent at commit 4b5600b)
note as N_ABSENT
  Primitives the project does NOT have today:
  - CCD soft-replug (SetDisplayConfig deactivate/reactivate). CCD.cs has
    only the read-only trio.
  - PnPCycle (SetupDi disable/enable). No PnPDeviceService.cs.
  - ElevationService / AllowPnPRecovery setting / install-elevation-task.
  - VCP 0x04 factory reset (user-excluded per feedback memory).
  Hard power-off VCP 0xD6 is user-initiated only (Ctrl+click).
end note

@enduml
